# CTC Server REST API Test File
# Use with VS Code REST Client extension or IntelliJ HTTP Client
#
# Usage:
#   - VS Code: Install "REST Client" extension by Huachao Mao
#   - IntelliJ: Built-in HTTP Client support
#   - Click "Send Request" above each request to execute

@baseUrl = http://192.168.10.19:3000

### ============================================================
### TEMPERATURE ENDPOINTS
### ============================================================

### Get current room temperature
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/temperature/room

### Get room temperature setpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/temperature/room/setpoint

### Set room temperature setpoint
# Note: Trailing slash required for POST
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/temperature/room/setpoint/?value=21.5

### Get outdoor temperature
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/temperature/outdoor

### Get flow temperature (heating circuit)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/temperature/flow

### Get return temperature (heating circuit return)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/temperature/flow/return

### ============================================================
### SMARTGRID ENDPOINTS
### ============================================================

### Get current SmartGrid mode
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/smartgrid

### Set SmartGrid mode to Normal
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/smartgrid?mode=normal

### Set SmartGrid mode to Blocking (power save / stop heating)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/smartgrid?mode=blocking

### Set SmartGrid mode to LowPrice (prioritize cheap energy)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/smartgrid?mode=lowprice

### Set SmartGrid mode to Overcapacity (maximum operation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/smartgrid?mode=overcapacity

### ============================================================
### POWER SAVE ENDPOINTS
### ============================================================

### Get power save status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ctc/powersave

### Enable power save mode (uses SmartGrid Blocking)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ctc/powersave?active=true

### Disable power save mode (returns to Normal)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ctc/powersave?active=false

### ============================================================
### CIRKULATIONSPUMP (via Homey)
### ============================================================
# Returns 503 when [homey].enabled = false in config.

### Get circulation pump state
# { "on": true|false|null, "stale": bool, "last_observed_unix_secs": int|null }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/pump

### ============================================================
### VISIBILITY REGISTER ENDPOINTS
### ============================================================

### Get all visibility registers (62500-62548)
# Returns all 49 visibility registers with their bitmask values
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/visibility

### Check if a specific BMS parameter is visible
# Example: HEATSYSTEM_ROOM_SETTEMP (register 61509)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/visibility/parameter/61509

### Check visibility of outdoor temperature parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/visibility/parameter/62000

### Check visibility of alarm count parameter (always visible)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/visibility/parameter/65001

### Check visibility of unknown parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/visibility/parameter/64000

### Read visibility register 62500 (first register)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/visibility/62500

### Read visibility register 62510
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/visibility/62510

### Read visibility register 62520
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/visibility/62520

### Read visibility register 62548 (last register)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/visibility/62548

### ============================================================
### GENERIC CTC PARAMETER ENDPOINTS
### ============================================================

### Read a known CTC parameter by address
# Example: Current room temperature (register 62203)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ctc?addr=62203

### Read outdoor temperature
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ctc?addr=62000

### Read flow temperature
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ctc?addr=62011

### Read a custom CTC parameter with factor
# Example: Custom register with 0.1 scaling factor
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ctc?addr=62203&factor=0.1&custom=true

### Write a CTC parameter by address
# Example: Set room temperature setpoint (register 61509) to 22.0
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ctc?addr=61509&value=22.0

### Set heating inclination
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ctc?addr=61513&value=1.5

### ============================================================
### COMMON CTC REGISTER ADDRESSES (for reference)
### ============================================================
#
# Temperature Registers (read-only):
#   62203 - CTC_ROOM_TEMP (Current room temp 1)
#   62000 - CTC_OUTDOOR_TEMP (Outdoor temperature)
#   62011 - HEATSYSTEM_FLOW_TEMP (Primary flow temperature)
#   62015 - CTC_RETURN_TEMP (Return temp)
#
# Setpoint Registers (read-write):
#   61509 - HEATSYSTEM_ROOM_SETTEMP (Set room temperature)
#   61513 - HEATSYSTEM_INCLINATION (Change inclination)
#   61517 - HEATSYSTEM_ADJUSTMENT (Change adjustment)
#   61534 - HEATSYSTEM_FLOW_MAX_TEMP (Max primary flow)
#   61538 - HEATSYSTEM_FLOW_MIN_TEMP (Min primary flow)
#
# Status/Mode Registers:
#   61542 - HEATSYSTEM_HEATING_MODE
#   1100  - SmartGrid control register
#
# Visibility Registers:
#   62500-62548 - Hardware capability bitmasks (49 registers)
#
# Alarm Registers:
#   65001 - Alarm/info count (low byte=alarms, high byte=infos)
#   65010-65059 - Alarm bitmask (800 alarms)
#   65060-65069 - Info bitmask (160 info messages)
#   65100 - Text buffer transfer register (write-only)
#   65101-65125 - ASCII text buffer (50 characters)
#
### ============================================================

### ============================================================
### ALARM ENDPOINTS
### ============================================================

### Get alarm status (quick check for polling)
# Returns alarm and info counts - fast, suitable for frequent polling
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alarms/status

### Get all active alarms and info messages with full details
# Returns parsed alarm/info messages with codes and English translations
# Note: Slower than /status as it reads text buffers for each active alarm
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/alarms

### ============================================================
